IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation: Part 3 Division 2, ss 30, 31 and 32 (conversion between kinds of company; default in complying with requirements as to private companies).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). s 30(4)(a)(iii) and (iv), s 32(1), s 32(2)(b) and s 32(7) are shown as deleted and are not encoded (NOTES.md, coverage table).
-- SEAM (PLAN.md section 4, table A). The keel's s 4(1) "private company" takes two facts that this module answers:
--   the input `the company was converted into a private company pursuant to section 31(1)` is answered by `s 31(3) the company has become a private company` (JUST TRUE);
--   the input `the company has ceased to be a private company under section 31 or 32` is answered by `s 31(3) the company has become a public company` or `s 32(3)(a) the company is a public company on and from the date specified` (JUST TRUE of either).
-- Answers: JUST TRUE (the test is met), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (the text does not say). See the header of sgi-capacity.l4.

§ `Section 30(1) and (2): changing between unlimited and limited`

-- (1): "Subject to this section — (a) an unlimited company may convert to a limited company if it was not previously a limited company that became an unlimited company pursuant to paragraph (b); and (b) a limited company may convert to an unlimited company if it was not previously an unlimited company that became a limited company pursuant to paragraph (a) or any corresponding previous written law."
-- A "may" gated by "if": NOTHING where the gate fails (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line F-I2).
-- src:5355 | (a) an unlimited company may convert to a limited company if
-- src:5356 | it was not previously a limited company that became an
-- src:5357 | unlimited company pursuant to paragraph (b); and
@ref s 30(1)(a) (src:5355-5357)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `it was previously a limited company that became an unlimited company pursuant to paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(1)(a) the unlimited company may convert to a limited company` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "unlimited company" the company is an unlimited company` liability EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF (NOT `it was previously a limited company that became an unlimited company pursuant to paragraph (b)`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an unlimited company may convert to a limited company if it was not previously a limited company that became an unlimited company pursuant to paragraph (b)" -- a power whose "if" gate failed (fork line F-I2)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) speaks of "an unlimited company"

-- src:5359 | (b) a limited company may convert to an unlimited company if
-- src:5360 | it was not previously an unlimited company that became a
-- src:5361 | limited company pursuant to paragraph (a) or any
-- src:5362 | corresponding previous written law.
@ref s 30(1)(b) (src:5359-5362)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was previously an unlimited company that became a limited company pursuant to paragraph (a) or any corresponding previous written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(1)(b) the limited company may convert to an unlimited company` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "limited company" the company is a limited company` liability `the period of 2 years specified in section 17(6) has expired` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF (NOT `it was previously an unlimited company that became a limited company pursuant to paragraph (a) or any corresponding previous written law`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a limited company may convert to an unlimited company if it was not previously an unlimited company that became a limited company pursuant to paragraph (a) ..." -- a power whose "if" gate failed (fork line F-I2)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) speaks of "a limited company"

-- (2): "Where a company applies to the Registrar for a change of status as provided by subsection (1) and, subject to section 33(8) and (9) as applied by subsection (7), lodges with the application the prescribed documents relating to the application,
-- the Registrar must, upon registration of such prescribed documents so lodged as are registrable under this Act, issue to the company a notice of incorporation — (a) appropriate to the change of status applied for; and (b) specifying ... that the notice is issued pursuant to this section,
-- and, upon the issue of such a notice of incorporation, the company is deemed to be a company having the status specified therein."
-- The Registrar's duty, read for what it means to the company. A duty gated by "Where" and "upon": JUST FALSE where a gate fails (fork line F-I21).
-- src:5367 | (2) Where a company applies to the Registrar for a change of status
-- src:5368 | as provided by subsection (1) and, subject to section 33(8) and (9) as
-- src:5369 | applied by subsection (7), lodges with the application the prescribed
-- src:5370 | documents relating to the application, the Registrar must, upon
-- src:5371 | registration of such prescribed documents so lodged as are registrable
-- src:5372 | under this Act, issue to the company a notice of incorporation —
-- src:5374 | (a) appropriate to the change of status applied for; and
-- src:5376 | (b) specifying, in addition to the particulars prescribed in
-- src:5377 | respect of a notice of incorporation of a company of that
-- src:5378 | status, that the notice is issued pursuant to this section,
-- src:5380 | and, upon the issue of such a notice of incorporation, the company is
-- src:5381 | deemed to be a company having the status specified therein.
@ref s 30(2) (src:5367-5381)
GIVEN `the company has applied to the Registrar for a change of status as provided by subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged with the application the prescribed documents relating to the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed documents so lodged as are registrable under this Act have been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(2) the Registrar must issue to the company a notice of incorporation appropriate to the change of status` MEANS
    IF    `the company has applied to the Registrar for a change of status as provided by subsection (1)`
      AND `the company has lodged with the application the prescribed documents relating to the application`
      AND `the prescribed documents so lodged as are registrable under this Act have been registered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company applies ... and ... lodges with the application the prescribed documents ..., the Registrar must, upon registration of such prescribed documents ..., issue to the company a notice of incorporation" (a duty gated by "Where" and "upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I21)

-- src:5367 | (2) Where a company applies to the Registrar for a change of status
-- src:5368 | as provided by subsection (1) and, subject to section 33(8) and (9) as
-- src:5369 | applied by subsection (7), lodges with the application the prescribed
-- src:5370 | documents relating to the application, the Registrar must, upon
-- src:5371 | registration of such prescribed documents so lodged as are registrable
-- src:5372 | under this Act, issue to the company a notice of incorporation —
-- src:5374 | (a) appropriate to the change of status applied for; and
-- src:5376 | (b) specifying, in addition to the particulars prescribed in
-- src:5377 | respect of a notice of incorporation of a company of that
-- src:5378 | status, that the notice is issued pursuant to this section,
-- src:5380 | and, upon the issue of such a notice of incorporation, the company is
-- src:5381 | deemed to be a company having the status specified therein.
@ref s 30(2) (src:5367-5381)
GIVEN `the Registrar has issued the notice of incorporation specifying that it is issued pursuant to section 30` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was issued` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(2) the company is deemed to be a company having the status specified in the notice` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has issued the notice of incorporation specifying that it is issued pursuant to section 30` AND `the date asked` AT LEAST `the day the notice was issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon the issue of such a notice of incorporation, the company is deemed to be a company having the status specified therein" (a status gated by "upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I11)

-- (3): "Where the status of a company is changed pursuant to this section, notice of the change of status must be published in such manner (if any) as the Registrar may direct."
-- Whether notice must be published where the Registrar directs no manner is not said: the "(if any)" leaves it open (NOTHING; fork line F-I26).
-- src:5383 | (3) Where the status of a company is changed pursuant to this
-- src:5384 | section, notice of the change of status must be published in such
-- src:5385 | manner (if any) as the Registrar may direct.
@ref s 30(3) (src:5383-5385)
GIVEN `the status of the company has been changed pursuant to section 30` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has directed a manner of publication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(3) the notice of the change of status must be published` MEANS
    IF `the status of the company has been changed pursuant to section 30`
    THEN (IF `the Registrar has directed a manner of publication`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "in such manner (if any) as the Registrar may direct" -- where the Registrar directs no manner the text does not say whether publication is still required (fork line F-I26)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the status of a company is changed pursuant to this section, notice of the change of status must be published" (a duty gated by "Where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-I21)

-- (3A): "Upon the application of the company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the incorporation of the company with the new status."
-- src:5387 | (3A) Upon the application of the company and payment of the
-- src:5388 | prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate
-- src:5389 | confirming the incorporation of the company with the new status.
@ref s 30(3A) (src:5387-5389)
GIVEN `the company has applied for the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(3A) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the incorporation with the new status` MEANS
    IF `the company has applied for the certificate` AND `the prescribed fee has been paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the application of the company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate" (a gate with "Upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I11)

§ `Section 30(4): the prescribed documents`

-- (4): "In subsection (2), 'prescribed documents', in relation to an application mentioned in that subsection, means — (a) a copy of a special resolution of the company — (i) resolving to change the status of the company and specifying the status sought;
-- (ii) making such alterations to the constitution of the company as are necessary to bring the constitution into conformity with the requirements of this Act relating to the constitution of a company of the status sought; and ... (v) changing the name of the company to a name by which it could be registered if it were a company of the status sought;
-- (b) where, by a special resolution mentioned in paragraph (a), the constitution of the company is altered or added to — a copy of the constitution as altered; and (c) in the case of an application by a limited company to convert to an unlimited company — (i) the prescribed form of assent to the application subscribed by or on behalf of all the members of the company; and
-- (ii) a declaration by or on behalf of a director or the secretary of the company, or a registered qualified individual authorised by the company, verifying that the persons by whom or on whose behalf such a form of assent is subscribed constitute the whole membership of the company and, if a member has not subscribed the form himself or herself, that the director, secretary or registered qualified individual making the declaration has taken all reasonable steps ..."
-- A "means" definition: closed. JUST TRUE where all the lodged documents are there; JUST FALSE otherwise.
-- src:5393 | (4) In subsection (2), “prescribed documents”, in relation to an
-- src:5394 | application mentioned in that subsection, means —
-- src:5396 | (a) a copy of a special resolution of the company —
-- src:5398 | (i) resolving to change the status of the company and
-- src:5399 | specifying the status sought;
-- src:5401 | (ii) making such alterations to the constitution of the
-- src:5402 | company as are necessary to bring the constitution
-- src:5403 | into conformity with the requirements of this Act
-- src:5404 | relating to the constitution of a company of the status
-- src:5405 | sought; and
-- src:5407 | (iii) [Deleted by Act 36 of 2014]
-- src:5409 | (iv) [Deleted by Act 36 of 2014]
-- src:5411 | (v) changing the name of the company to a name by
-- src:5412 | which it could be registered if it were a company of
-- src:5413 | the status sought;
-- src:5418 | (b) where, by a special resolution mentioned in paragraph (a),
-- src:5419 | the constitution of the company is altered or added to — a
-- src:5420 | copy of the constitution as altered; and
-- src:5422 | (c) in the case of an application by a limited company to
-- src:5423 | convert to an unlimited company —
-- src:5425 | (i) the prescribed form of assent to the application
-- src:5426 | subscribed by or on behalf of all the members of the
-- src:5427 | company; and
-- src:5429 | (ii) a declaration by or on behalf of a director or the
-- src:5430 | secretary of the company, or a registered qualified
-- src:5431 | individual authorised by the company, verifying that
-- src:5432 | the persons by whom or on whose behalf such a form
-- src:5433 | of assent is subscribed constitute the whole
-- src:5434 | membership of the company and, if a member has
-- src:5435 | not subscribed the form himself or herself, that the
-- src:5436 | director, secretary or registered qualified individual
-- src:5437 | making the declaration has taken all reasonable steps
-- src:5438 | to satisfy himself or herself that each person who
-- src:5439 | subscribed the form was lawfully empowered to do
-- src:5440 | so.
@ref s 30(4) (src:5393-5440)
GIVEN `the application is by a limited company to convert to an unlimited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of a special resolution is lodged resolving to change the status of the company and specifying the status sought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special resolution makes such alterations to the constitution as are necessary to bring it into conformity with the requirements of this Act for a company of the status sought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special resolution changes the name of the company to a name by which it could be registered if it were a company of the status sought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the company is altered or added to by the special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the constitution as altered is lodged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed form of assent subscribed by or on behalf of all the members of the company is lodged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a declaration verifying the whole membership and the reasonable steps taken is lodged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(4) the documents lodged are the prescribed documents` MEANS
    IF    `a copy of a special resolution is lodged resolving to change the status of the company and specifying the status sought`
      AND `the special resolution makes such alterations to the constitution as are necessary to bring it into conformity with the requirements of this Act for a company of the status sought`
      AND `the special resolution changes the name of the company to a name by which it could be registered if it were a company of the status sought`
      AND ((NOT `the constitution of the company is altered or added to by the special resolution`) OR `a copy of the constitution as altered is lodged`)
      AND ((NOT `the application is by a limited company to convert to an unlimited company`) OR (`the prescribed form of assent subscribed by or on behalf of all the members of the company is lodged` AND `a declaration verifying the whole membership and the reasonable steps taken is lodged`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'prescribed documents' ... means — (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." (a "means" definition: a document missing from the list is not within it)

§ `Section 30(5) to (8): the effect of the change of status`

-- (5): "Section 26(2) to (6) does not apply to or in relation to an application under this section or to any prescribed documents in relation to the application."
-- src:5444 | (5) Section 26(2) to (6) does not apply to or in relation to an
-- src:5445 | application under this section or to any prescribed documents in
-- src:5446 | relation to the application.
@ref s 30(5) (src:5444-5446)
GIVEN `the matter is an application under section 30 or prescribed documents in relation to the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(5) section 26(2) to (6) applies to the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter is an application under section 30 or prescribed documents in relation to the application`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 26(2) to (6) does not apply to or in relation to an application under this section or to any prescribed documents in relation to the application."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection excludes an application under section 30 and its prescribed documents and says nothing of any other matter

-- (6): "A special resolution passed for the purposes of an application under this section takes effect only upon the issue under this section of a notice of incorporation of the company to which the resolution relates."
-- src:5448 | (6) A special resolution passed for the purposes of an application
-- src:5449 | under this section takes effect only upon the issue under this section
-- src:5450 | of a notice of incorporation of the company to which the resolution
-- src:5451 | relates.
@ref s 30(6) (src:5448-5451)
GIVEN `the special resolution was passed for the purposes of an application under section 30` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has issued under section 30 a notice of incorporation of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was issued` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(6) the special resolution has taken effect` MEANS
    IF `the special resolution was passed for the purposes of an application under section 30`
    THEN (IF `the Registrar has issued under section 30 a notice of incorporation of the company` AND `the date asked` AT LEAST `the day the notice was issued`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "takes effect only upon the issue under this section of a notice of incorporation" (a gate closed with "only upon")
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A special resolution passed for the purposes of an application under this section" -- another resolution is outside the subsection

-- (7): "With such modifications as may be necessary, section 33 (except subsection (1)) applies to and in respect of the proposal, passing and lodging, and the cancellation or confirmation by the Court, of a special resolution relating to a change of status as if it were a special resolution under that section."
-- Whether section 33 applies is answered; what the "modifications as may be necessary" are is not said (fork line F-I27).
-- src:5453 | (7) With such modifications as may be necessary, section 33
-- src:5454 | (except subsection (1)) applies to and in respect of the proposal,
-- src:5455 | passing and lodging, and the cancellation or confirmation by the
-- src:5456 | Court, of a special resolution relating to a change of status as if it were
-- src:5457 | a special resolution under that section.
@ref s 30(7) (src:5453-5457)
GIVEN `the special resolution relates to a change of status` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is section 33(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(7) the provision of section 33 applies to the special resolution` MEANS
    IF `the special resolution relates to a change of status`
    THEN (IF `the provision is section 33(1)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "section 33 (except subsection (1))"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- "With such modifications as may be necessary" (fork line F-I27)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a special resolution relating to a change of status" -- another resolution is outside the subsection

DECLARE `s 30(8) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 30(8)(a) the creation of a new legal entity`
    `s 30(8)(b) the identity of the body corporate constituted by the company or its continuity as a body corporate`
    `s 30(8)(c) the property, or the rights or obligations, of the company`
    `s 30(8)(d) the validity of legal proceedings by or against the company`
    `s 30(8) another matter`

-- (8): "A change in the status of a company pursuant to this section does not operate — (a) to create a new legal entity; (b) to prejudice or affect the identity of the body corporate constituted by the company or its continuity as a body corporate; (c) to affect the property, or the rights or obligations, of the company; or (d) to render defective any legal proceedings by or against the company".
-- src:5459 | (8) A change in the status of a company pursuant to this section
-- src:5460 | does not operate —
-- src:5465 | (a) to create a new legal entity;
-- src:5467 | (b) to prejudice or affect the identity of the body corporate
-- src:5468 | constituted by the company or its continuity as a body
-- src:5469 | corporate;
-- src:5471 | (c) to affect the property, or the rights or obligations, of the
-- src:5472 | company; or
-- src:5474 | (d) to render defective any legal proceedings by or against the
-- src:5475 | company,
@ref s 30(8) (src:5459-5475)
GIVEN `the status of the company was changed pursuant to section 30` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 30(8) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(8) the change in status operates on the matter` MEANS
    IF `the status of the company was changed pursuant to section 30`
    THEN (IF matter EQUALS `s 30(8) another matter`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names four matters and says nothing of any other
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not operate — (a) to create a new legal entity; (b) ...; (c) ...; or (d) ..."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A change in the status of a company pursuant to this section" -- a change made another way is outside the subsection

-- (8), second limb: "any legal proceedings that could have been continued or commenced by or against it prior to the change in its status may, despite the change in its status, be continued or commenced by or against it after the change in its status."
-- src:5459 | (8) A change in the status of a company pursuant to this section
-- src:5460 | does not operate —
-- src:5465 | (a) to create a new legal entity;
-- src:5467 | (b) to prejudice or affect the identity of the body corporate
-- src:5468 | constituted by the company or its continuity as a body
-- src:5469 | corporate;
-- src:5471 | (c) to affect the property, or the rights or obligations, of the
-- src:5472 | company; or
-- src:5474 | (d) to render defective any legal proceedings by or against the
-- src:5475 | company,
-- src:5477 | and any legal proceedings that could have been continued or
-- src:5478 | commenced by or against it prior to the change in its status may,
-- src:5479 | despite the change in its status, be continued or commenced by or
-- src:5480 | against it after the change in its status.
@ref s 30(8) (src:5459-5480)
GIVEN `the status of the company was changed pursuant to section 30` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legal proceedings could have been continued or commenced by or against the company prior to the change in its status` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(8) the legal proceedings may be continued or commenced by or against the company after the change in its status` MEANS
    IF `the status of the company was changed pursuant to section 30` AND `the legal proceedings could have been continued or commenced by or against the company prior to the change in its status`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any legal proceedings that could have been continued or commenced ... prior to the change in its status may ... be continued or commenced ... after" -- a permission whose conditions are not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

§ `Section 31(1) to (3): converting between private and public`

-- (1): "A public company having a share capital may convert to a private company by lodging with the Registrar — (a) a copy of a special resolution — (i) determining to convert to a private company and specifying an appropriate alteration to its name; and (ii) altering the provisions of its constitution so far as is necessary to impose the restrictions and limitations referred to in section 18(1);
-- (b) a list of persons holding shares in the company in the prescribed form; and (c) such other information relating to the company or its members and officers as may be prescribed."
-- The way is lodging: a permission whose conditions are not met names no outcome (NOTHING; fork line F-I2).
-- src:5484 | 31.—(1) A public company having a share capital may convert to a
-- src:5485 | private company by lodging with the Registrar —
-- src:5487 | (a) a copy of a special resolution —
-- src:5489 | (i) determining to convert to a private company and
-- src:5490 | specifying an appropriate alteration to its name; and
-- src:5492 | (ii) altering the provisions of its constitution so far as is
-- src:5493 | necessary to impose the restrictions and limitations
-- src:5494 | referred to in section 18(1);
-- src:5496 | (b) a list of persons holding shares in the company in the
-- src:5497 | prescribed form; and
-- src:5499 | (c) such other information relating to the company or its
-- src:5500 | members and officers as may be prescribed.
@ref s 31(1) (src:5484-5500)
GIVEN `the company is a public company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company lodges a copy of a special resolution determining to convert to a private company and specifying an appropriate alteration to its name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special resolution alters the provisions of its constitution so far as is necessary to impose the restrictions and limitations referred to in section 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company lodges a list of persons holding shares in the company in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company lodges such other information relating to the company or its members and officers as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(1) the public company may convert to a private company by lodging` MEANS
    IF    `the company is a public company having a share capital`
      AND `the company lodges a copy of a special resolution determining to convert to a private company and specifying an appropriate alteration to its name`
      AND `the special resolution alters the provisions of its constitution so far as is necessary to impose the restrictions and limitations referred to in section 18(1)`
      AND `the company lodges a list of persons holding shares in the company in the prescribed form`
      AND `the company lodges such other information relating to the company or its members and officers as may be prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company having a share capital may convert to a private company by lodging with the Registrar — (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." -- a permission whose subject or lodging is not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

-- (2): "A private company may, subject to its constitution, convert to a public company by lodging with the Registrar — (a) a copy of a special resolution determining to convert to a public company and specifying an appropriate alteration to its name; (b) a statement in lieu of prospectus; and (c) a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that section 61(2)(b) has been complied with,
-- and thereupon the restrictions and limitations referred to in section 18(1) as included in or deemed to be included in the constitution of such company cease to form part of the constitution."
-- src:5504 | Change from private to public company
-- src:5506 | (2) A private company may, subject to its constitution, convert to a
-- src:5507 | public company by lodging with the Registrar —
-- src:5509 | (a) a copy of a special resolution determining to convert to a
-- src:5510 | public company and specifying an appropriate alteration to
-- src:5511 | its name;
-- src:5516 | (b) a statement in lieu of prospectus; and
-- src:5518 | (c) a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that
-- src:5519 | section 61(2)(b) has been complied with,
-- src:5521 | and thereupon the restrictions and limitations referred to in
-- src:5522 | section 18(1) as included in or deemed to be included in the
-- src:5523 | constitution of such company cease to form part of the constitution.
@ref s 31(2) (src:5504-5523)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its constitution does not bar the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company lodges a copy of a special resolution determining to convert to a public company and specifying an appropriate alteration to its name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company lodges a statement in lieu of prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company lodges a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that section 61(2)(b) has been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(2) the private company may convert to a public company by lodging` MEANS
    IF    `the company is a private company`
      AND `its constitution does not bar the conversion`
      AND `the company lodges a copy of a special resolution determining to convert to a public company and specifying an appropriate alteration to its name`
      AND `the company lodges a statement in lieu of prospectus`
      AND `the company lodges a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that section 61(2)(b) has been complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company may, subject to its constitution, convert to a public company by lodging with the Registrar — (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." -- a permission whose subject, constitution or lodging is not met; the text names no outcome (fork line F-I2)

