    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On compliance by a company with ... subsection (2) and on the issue of a notice of incorporation altered accordingly the company becomes ... a public company" (a status gated by "On": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I11)

§ `Section 31(3A) to (5): the list of shareholders, the effect, and the certificate`

-- (3A): "The public company referred to in subsection (2) must, within 14 days after the issue of the notice of incorporation referred to in subsection (3), lodge with the Registrar in the prescribed form a list of persons holding shares in the company."
-- Lodged within the 14 days (P2: an act on any day up to the last day is in time): JUST TRUE; lodged late, or not lodged after the last day: JUST FALSE; not lodged and the 14 days not yet run: NOTHING.
-- src:5532 | (3A) The public company referred to in subsection (2) must, within
-- src:5533 | 14 days after the issue of the notice of incorporation referred to in
-- src:5534 | subsection (3), lodge with the Registrar in the prescribed form a list of
-- src:5535 | persons holding shares in the company.
@ref s 31(3A) (src:5532-5535)
GIVEN `the company is the public company referred to in subsection (2) and the notice of incorporation referred to in subsection (3) has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was issued` IS A DATE
      `the company has lodged the list with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company lodged the list` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(3A) the company has complied with the duty to lodge the list of persons holding shares` MEANS
    IF `the company is the public company referred to in subsection (2) and the notice of incorporation referred to in subsection (3) has been issued`
    THEN (IF `the company has lodged the list with the Registrar`
          THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the notice was issued` `the day the company lodged the list` 14 Days
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within 14 days after the issue of the notice of incorporation ..., lodge" (a period the text fixes in its own words, outside it)
          ELSE (IF `the date asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the notice was issued` 14 Days
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the 14 days have run and nothing is lodged
                ELSE NOTHING))    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 14 days have not run, and the text does not say the duty is met or unmet before then
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The public company referred to in subsection (2)" -- another company is outside the subsection

DECLARE `s 31(3A) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 31(3A) lodge with the Registrar in the prescribed form a list of persons holding shares in the company`

-- The duty as a regulative rule. Time 0 is the day the notice of incorporation is issued.
-- src:5532 | (3A) The public company referred to in subsection (2) must, within
-- src:5533 | 14 days after the issue of the notice of incorporation referred to in
-- src:5534 | subsection (3), lodge with the Registrar in the prescribed form a list of
-- src:5535 | persons holding shares in the company.
@ref s 31(3A) (src:5532-5535)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 31(3A) act`
`s 31(3A) the company must lodge the list of persons holding shares within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 31(3A) lodge with the Registrar in the prescribed form a list of persons holding shares in the company`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge with the Registrar a list of persons holding shares within 14 days after the notice of incorporation was issued"

DECLARE `s 31(4) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 31(4)(a) the identity of the company`
    `s 31(4)(b) the rights or obligations of the company`
    `s 31(4)(c) the validity of legal proceedings by or against the company`
    `s 31(4) another matter`

-- (4): "A conversion of a company pursuant to subsection (1) or (2) does not affect the identity of the company or any rights or obligations of the company or render defective any legal proceedings by or against the company".
-- src:5539 | (4) A conversion of a company pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)
-- src:5540 | does not affect the identity of the company or any rights or
-- src:5541 | obligations of the company or render defective any legal
-- src:5542 | proceedings by or against the company, and any legal proceedings
-- src:5543 | that could have been continued or commenced by or against it prior to
-- src:5544 | the conversion may, despite any change in the company’s name or
-- src:5545 | capacity in consequence of the conversion, be continued or
-- src:5546 | commenced by or against it after the conversion.
@ref s 31(4) (src:5539-5546)
GIVEN `the company was converted pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 31(4) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(4) the conversion affects the matter` MEANS
    IF `the company was converted pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN (IF matter EQUALS `s 31(4) another matter`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names the identity, the rights or obligations and the legal proceedings, and says nothing of any other matter
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the identity of the company or any rights or obligations of the company or render defective any legal proceedings by or against the company"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A conversion of a company pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)" -- a conversion made another way is outside the subsection

-- src:5539 | (4) A conversion of a company pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)
-- src:5540 | does not affect the identity of the company or any rights or
-- src:5541 | obligations of the company or render defective any legal
-- src:5542 | proceedings by or against the company, and any legal proceedings
-- src:5543 | that could have been continued or commenced by or against it prior to
-- src:5544 | the conversion may, despite any change in the company’s name or
-- src:5545 | capacity in consequence of the conversion, be continued or
-- src:5546 | commenced by or against it after the conversion.
@ref s 31(4) (src:5539-5546)
GIVEN `the company was converted pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legal proceedings could have been continued or commenced by or against the company prior to the conversion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(4) the legal proceedings may be continued or commenced by or against the company after the conversion` MEANS
    IF `the company was converted pursuant to subsection (1) or (2)` AND `the legal proceedings could have been continued or commenced by or against the company prior to the conversion`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any legal proceedings that could have been continued or commenced by or against it prior to the conversion may, despite any change in the company's name or capacity in consequence of the conversion, be continued or commenced by or against it after the conversion" -- a permission whose conditions are not met (fork line F-I2)

-- (5): "Upon the application of the company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the incorporation of the company with the new status."
-- src:5548 | (5) Upon the application of the company and payment of the
-- src:5549 | prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate
-- src:5550 | confirming the incorporation of the company with the new status.
@ref s 31(5) (src:5548-5550)
GIVEN `the company has applied for the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(5) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the incorporation with the new status` MEANS
    IF `the company has applied for the certificate` AND `the prescribed fee has been paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the application of the company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate" (a gate with "Upon": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork line F-I11)

§ `Section 32: default in complying with requirements as to private companies`

-- (2): "Where — (a) default has been made in relation to a private company in complying with a limitation of a kind specified in section 18(1)(b) that is included, or is deemed to be included in the constitution of the company; (c) the constitution of a private company have been so altered that they no longer include restrictions or limitations of the kinds specified in section 18(1); or
-- (d) a private company has ceased to have a share capital, the Registrar may by notice served on the company determine that, on such date as is specified in the notice, the company ceased to be a private company."
-- A "may" gated by "Where": NOTHING when the gate fails (grant ruling, limit 1; split site (ii), fork line F-I19).
-- src:5559 | (2) Where —
-- src:5561 | (a) default has been made in relation to a private company in
-- src:5562 | complying with a limitation of a kind specified in
-- src:5567 | section 18(1)(b) that is included, or is deemed to be
-- src:5568 | included in the constitution of the company;
-- src:5570 | (b) [Deleted by Act 5 of 2004]
-- src:5572 | (c) the constitution of a private company have been so altered
-- src:5573 | that they no longer include restrictions or limitations of the
-- src:5574 | kinds specified in section 18(1); or
-- src:5576 | (d) a private company has ceased to have a share capital,
-- src:5578 | the Registrar may by notice served on the company determine that, on
-- src:5579 | such date as is specified in the notice, the company ceased to be a
-- src:5580 | private company.
@ref s 32(2) (src:5559-5580)
GIVEN `default has been made in relation to a private company in complying with a limitation of a kind specified in section 18(1)(b) that is included or deemed to be included in its constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the private company has been so altered that it no longer includes restrictions or limitations of the kinds specified in section 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the private company has ceased to have a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(2) the Registrar may by notice served on the company determine that it ceased to be a private company` MEANS
    IF    `default has been made in relation to a private company in complying with a limitation of a kind specified in section 18(1)(b) that is included or deemed to be included in its constitution`
       OR `the constitution of the private company has been so altered that it no longer includes restrictions or limitations of the kinds specified in section 18(1)`
       OR `the private company has ceased to have a share capital`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where — (a) ...; (c) ...; or (d) ..., the Registrar may by notice served on the company determine" -- a power gated by "Where"; split site (ii), fork line F-I19

-- (3), paragraph (a): "Where, under this section, the Court or the Registrar determines that a company has ceased to be a private company — (a) the company is a public company and is deemed to have been a public company on and from the date specified in the order or notice".
-- The status is the date-specified one: before that date the text does not make the company public (JUST FALSE; fork line F-I28). This is the seam answer for "ceased to be a private company under section 31 or 32".
-- src:5587 | (a) the company is a public company and is deemed to have
-- src:5588 | been a public company on and from the date specified in
-- src:5589 | the order or notice;
@ref s 32(3)(a) (src:5587-5589)
