      `the date specified in the order or notice` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(3)(a) the company is a public company on and from the date specified` MEANS
    IF `the Court or the Registrar has determined under section 32 that the company has ceased to be a private company` AND `the date asked` AT LEAST `the date specified in the order or notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, under this section, the Court or the Registrar determines that a company has ceased to be a private company — (a) the company is a public company and is deemed to have been a public company on and from the date specified in the order or notice" (a status gated by "Where" and fixed from a date: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (a) and (b); fork lines F-I21 and F-I28)

