    IF `the Court or the Registrar has determined under section 32 that the company has ceased to be a private company` AND `the date asked` AT LEAST `the date specified in the order or notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company is on the date so specified deemed to have changed its name by the omission from its name of the word 'Private' or the word 'Sendirian'" (a status gated by "Where" and fixed on a date: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (a) and (b); fork lines F-I21 and F-I28)

-- (3)(c): "the company must, within a period of 14 days after the date of the order or the notice, lodge with the Registrar — (i) a statement in lieu of prospectus; and (ii) a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that section 61(2)(b) has been complied with."
