      `the company has lodged the statement in lieu of prospectus and the declaration with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company completed the lodging` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32(3)(c) the company has complied with the duty to lodge the statement in lieu of prospectus and the declaration` MEANS
    IF `the Court or the Registrar has determined under section 32 that the company has ceased to be a private company`
    THEN (IF `the company has lodged the statement in lieu of prospectus and the declaration with the Registrar`
          THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day of the order or the notice` `the day the company completed the lodging` 14 Days
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within a period of 14 days after the date of the order or the notice, lodge" (a period the text fixes in its own words, outside it)
          ELSE (IF `the date asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the order or the notice` 14 Days
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the 14 days have run and nothing is lodged
                ELSE NOTHING))    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 14 days have not run, and the text does not say the duty is met or unmet before then
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, under this section, the Court or the Registrar determines that a company has ceased to be a private company — ... (c) the company must, within a period of 14 days ..., lodge" (a duty gated by "Where": the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2; fork line F-I21)

DECLARE `s 32(3)(c) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 32(3)(c) lodge with the Registrar a statement in lieu of prospectus and a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that section 61(2)(b) has been complied with`

-- The duty as a regulative rule. Time 0 is the date of the order or the notice. The two documents are one act: both are to be lodged within the 14 days.
