    IF `a default or alteration referred to in subsection (2) has occurred` AND `the Court is satisfied that it was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause or that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a public body's power, a failed gate; S1b ruling 2026S1bC): "Where the Court is satisfied that ..., the Court may ... determine that the company has not ceased to be a private company" -- the Court's power gated by "Where" and the gate fails; split site (ii), fork line F-I19 (the other reading is NOTHING, the grant rule)

-- (5): "A company that, by virtue of a determination made under this section, has become a public company may not convert to a private company without the permission of the Court."
