    IF `the company has become a public company by virtue of a determination made under section 32`
    THEN (IF `the Court has given permission`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "without the permission of the Court" is met; the text then says nothing of whether the company may convert (fork line F-I18)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company that, by virtue of a determination made under this section, has become a public company" -- another company is outside the subsection

